  "title": "The GitHub Secret That Breaks Claude's Limitations",
  "description": "A single file on a GitHub repo with almost 200,000 stars makes Claude noticeably better, because instead of telling the AI what to do it tells the AI what NOT to do: no over-engineering, no assumptions when confused, no random changes, and always double check the work before saying it is done. The free guide below has the full rules file, where exactly to put it, and before and after examples.\n\nGet the full guide here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T5EiQFW9HeU1e5s0Afp7Z1s5bBbZ3kuKdgZYk5CIzfY/edit?usp=sharing\n\n#Shorts #ClaudeAI #GitHub",
